 "definitions": "RULES R1 — performance_motion new measurements (2026-11-10 HKT).\n\nOne command:  python3 analyze_rules_r1_pm.py [--root <research>] [--out <dir>]\nRelative ROOT: research root = two levels above this script (override --root / R1_PM_ROOT).\nOutput default ../rules_r1_img (override --out / R1_PM_OUT).\nReads official images in place (read-only), verifies md5 against our I3 OFFICIAL table\n(same paths as REF v7 §8). Reuses read-only helpers from ../i3_scripts (not modified).\nNo colour-threshold hair masks (R3). Masks: alpha>=128 official matte, except\nEX14 nosword (tv_simplify v2 hand-polygon derived silhouette, white>=128) and\nEX05 official silhouette assets char_s / char_s2 (alpha>=16, same as I3).\n\nMeasures (definitions):\n  A. pose-vs-carrier silhouette IoU. Each mask tight-bbox cropped, height-normalised\n     to H=256 (NEAREST), placed on a common canvas with bbox bottoms aligned; horizontal\n     offset searched over +-38 px (15% H) to maximise IoU (removes placement bias).\n     IoU=|A&B|/|A|B| at the best offset. XOR share by bbox-height band\n     (0-22, 22-40, 40-60, 60-80, 80-100 %) = XOR pixels in band / total XOR.\n  B. aspect = bbox w/h on the native mask; area_over_h2 = area/h^2.\nStatic images only: nothing here is an animation, cloth or audience PASS.\n",
